2 METHODOLOGY
2.1 Overview
Fig. 1. Overview of Methodology
We use two single-stage fine-tuning baselines- Bilingual Fine-Tuning (B-FT) and Multilingual Fine-Tuning (M-FT) as
described in [41]. In B-FT we fine-tune one language pair at a time with domain-specific parallel data. Meanwhile, in
M-FT, we fine-tune more than one language pair simultaneously with domain-specific parallel data. M-FT is further
categorized into three types:
(1) Many-to-One Multilingual Fine-Tuning (M2O-FT): Many → Language X
(2) One-to-Many Multilingual Fine-Tuning (O2M-FT): Language X → Many
(3) Many-to-Many Multilingual Fine-Tuning (M2M-FT): Many → Many, with Language X as a pivot language.
