3.2 msLLM selection
For our experiments, we select mBART50. It supports all the considered languages. In particular, mBART has shown
promising results for supervised and unsupervised NMT [28, 41]. mBART is memory efficient and has shown relatively
better results than mT5 [25]. We follow the same mBART model architecture — the standard sequence-to-sequence
Transformer [43], with 12 layers of encoder-decoder with the model dimension of 1024 on 16 heads. For training, we
use the FairSeq10 tool.
