4.4 ITTL Fine-tuning
Results of our two ITTL strategies [biCPT,3-B-FT] and [triCPT, M-FT,B-FT] 20 are given in the last four raws of Table 5.
Three-stage fine-tuning ITTL [biCPT,3-B-FT] significantly improves BLEU score compared to baseline B-FT for all
the directions where we obtained a maximum of +1.81 score improvement for Si → T a and a minimum of +0.65
improvements on En → T a.
Our biCPT 3-stage fine-tuning results prove that utilizing the available in-domain monolingual and out-domain
parallel data enhances fine-tuning performance in extremely low-resource domain-specific settings rather than only
utilizing out-domain parallel data.
Our second ITTL approach, Fine-tuning from Multilingual Fine-tuned MNMT models [triCPT,M-FT,B-FT] shows
quantifiable improvements except on Si → En. For Si → T a and T a → Si, we obtain +1.41 and +1.83 BLEU score gains
respectively, and also notably +1.03 on En → T a direction.
Overall, we prove that utilizing additional in-domain monolingual data for pre-training and in- and out-domain
